# The marker sentence's cases, run by EVERY reader of it:
#
#   cerebro--session-args-p   (emacs/cerebro.el)    via emacs/cerebro-test.el
#   scripts/agent-alive       (bash)                via tests/agent-alive.sh
#   scripts/fleet-cost        (SQL and jq)          via tests/fleet-cost.sh
#
# The rule: a field is <name>'s session of the fleet at <root> when it carries cerebro's own
# marker sentence, which `scripts/launch' puts at the head of every session's prompt:
#
#   This session is <Name> of the cerebro fleet rooted at <root>/. This sentence is how the fleet
#   view proves the session belongs to this checkout; do not remove it.
#
# Two needles are cut from that one sentence - `This session is <name> of the cerebro fleet rooted
# at ' for the name, and `cerebro fleet rooted at <root>/' for the root - so the rule keeps the
# two-test shape `cerebro--session-liveness' builds its three answers on. No provider's flag
# spelling is evidence any more (cb-d59.3): `--name' is still passed, and proves nothing.
# Add a case here and EVERY suite runs it; a case one side answers differently is a divergence,
# which is what this file exists to make impossible. Before this table each side kept its own list
# and the two drifted, twice; the third reader was added without subscribing at all, invented its
# own fixture spellings, and reported a silent zero for a fleet that had spent ten thousand
# credits that week (cb-d89, cb-akt).
#
# A NEW READER SUBSCRIBES HERE *AND* DECLARES ITSELF IN `scripts/marker-readers' (cb-9su). This
# table only ever held the readers that opted in, so a reader that never subscribed was not red -
# it was silently wrong. That check is what makes the opt-in mandatory: it fails the gate on any
# file under scripts, emacs, tests, hooks or githooks that spells the sentence without a declared
# row naming its subscribing suite.
#
# THE FIELD IS NOT ALWAYS A COMMAND LINE. The row's last field is *the text a reader sees*: a
# process's command line for `scripts/agent-alive' and `cerebro--session-args-p', and turn 0's
# `user_message' for `scripts/fleet-cost'. `alive'/`dead' means *this field is NAME's session of
# the fleet at ROOT* - answered as a predicate by the first two, and by the third as: extract the
# name and the root from the field, and compare both.
#
# Format:  <alive|dead>  <name>  <{root}|{other}>  <the field>
#   - fields are separated by runs of blanks; the field is the rest of the line
#   - `\n' IN THE FIELD IS A NEWLINE, unescaped by every runner, and it is the only escape. A real
#     turn 0 is the marker, a blank line, then the instruction, and a line-based table cannot hold
#     that otherwise.
#   - NO APOSTROPHE IN ANY ROW: tests/fleet-cost.sh interpolates the field into a `sqlite3' string
#     literal, and scripts/launch avoids apostrophes in the marker for its own bash-3.2 reason.
#   - KEEP A ROW'S FIELD SHORT: scripts/agent-alive reads it back with `ps -o args='.
#   - <name> must be on the built-in roster (scripts/roster): the bash runner's fixture declares
#     no roster of its own, and agent-alive refuses a name it does not know
#   - {root}, {other} and {root}-hud are the three consumer roots the bash runner creates
#
# NOT here, because they are about how one side OBTAINS the args or the root, not about the rule:
# elisp's tilde-spelled and trailing-slash roots (consumer-root is always physical and absolute),
# and bash's no-state-file / no-pid / pid-not-an-integer / pid-exited / not-on-the-roster cases
# (process-attributes takes an integer, and elisp reads no roster here). Those stay in their suite.

# the launcher's own shape: alive in its consumer
alive  Cyclops  {root}   --agent implementer --name Cyclops --remote-control Cyclops --permission-mode auto This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {root}/. This sentence is how the fleet view proves the session belongs to this checkout; do not remove it.
alive  Cyclops  {root}   This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {root}/.
# the name: another agent's session, and a name that is only a prefix of the one in the args
dead   Beast    {root}   This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {root}/.
dead   Cyclops  {root}   This session is Cyclopsly of the cerebro fleet rooted at {root}/.
alive  Storm    {root}   --remote-control-session-name-prefix Cyclops --name Storm This session is Storm of the cerebro fleet rooted at {root}/.
# a Claude Code flag is no longer evidence: --name alone proves nothing now
dead   Cyclops  {root}   --name Cyclops
dead   Cyclops  {root}   --agent implementer --name Cyclops --remote-control Cyclops --permission-mode auto --settings {root}/.claude/cerebro/hooks/question-state.settings.json
# the root: another consumer, and a sibling checkout whose path merely starts with this one's
dead   Cyclops  {root}   This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {other}/.
alive  Cyclops  {other}  This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {other}/.
dead   Cyclops  {root}   This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {root}-hud/.
# the previous launcher's carrier, which the new rule still recognises: no flag day on merge
alive  Cyclops  {root}   --name Cyclops --append-system-prompt This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {root}/. This sentence is how the fleet view proves the session belongs to this checkout; do not remove it.
# the store's shape: the marker is the FIRST SENTENCE of a whole seed prompt, not the whole field.
# `\n' is a newline, so the row carries the blank line scripts/launch writes between the marker and
# the instruction. The second row is the probe fixture's shape - a session of another root - in
# prompt shape, so "wrong root" and "prompt shape" meet in one row rather than only separately.
alive  Cyclops  {root}   This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {root}/. This sentence is how the fleet view proves the session belongs to this checkout; do not remove it.\n\nYou are Cyclops.
dead   Cyclops  {root}   This session is Cyclops of the cerebro fleet rooted at {other}/. This sentence is how the fleet view proves the session belongs to this checkout; do not remove it.\n\nYou are Cyclops.
